{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZuu5SeJuF7AVHdT9WZv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete picture of the codebase. Let me compile my findings and move to DESIGN.\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add ability to cancel orders with status tracking, where ACTIVE orders transition to CANCELLED state, cancelling CREATED shipments, while rejecting cancellations with CONFIRMED shipments (409) and supporting idempotent repeated cancellations.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order model: `Order.kt:11` — currently lacks status field\n- OrderController: `OrderController.kt:15` — handles POST/GET /orders\n- OrderRepository: `OrderRepository.kt:10` — in-memory storage, no queries by orderId\n- Shipment model: `Shipment.kt:9` — has status enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentRepository: `ShipmentRepository.kt:10` — no findByOrderId method yet\n- ShipmentController: `ShipmentController.kt:20` — creates shipments without order validation\n- Error handling: `ApiExceptions.kt:11`, `ApiError.kt:31`, `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13`\n- ErrorCode enum: `ApiError.kt:31` — needs new codes for order cancellation\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- All errors thrown as ApiException subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException)\n- Error responses wrapped in ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n- In-memory repository pattern with save/findById/findAll/existsById/clear methods\n- Kotlin data classes for models\n- MockMvc tests checking both status and `$.error.code` in response\n- Controllers inject repositories and perform business logic inline\n\n**Affected files and why:**\n1. `Order.kt` — must add `status: OrderStatus` field to track ACTIVE/CANCELLED states\n2. `OrderController.kt` — must add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — must add `findByOrderId(orderId)` to query shipments by order\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — must validate order status before creating shipment\n5. `ApiError.kt` — must add `ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT` error code for CONFIRMED shipment conflict\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — must test all cancel scenarios (active→cancelled, idempotent, conflicts, not found)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Non-atomic cancel operation: checking shipments then updating order/shipments isn't transactional in-memory; but in-memory store is inherently single-threaded so this works\n- Missing findByOrderId in ShipmentRepository could cause N+1 queries; must add this method\n- Shipment creation must check order status but OrderRepository is separate; need to inject it into ShipmentController\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What error code for \"cannot cancel with CONFIRMED shipment\"? I'll use `ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT` per existing pattern\n- Should cancel return the updated Order? Yes, requirement says \"returns the order\"\n- What happens if you create a shipment for a non-existent order? Requirement says \"keeps its current behaviour\" — no validation today\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class. Create `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. Newly created orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order or throws ResourceNotFoundException\n   - If already CANCELLED, return it (idempotent)\n   - Check all shipments for that order; if any are CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT\n   - Update order status to CANCELLED\n   - Update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Save and return the cancelled order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to query shipments by order ID.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: Inject OrderRepository. Before creating shipment, check that order exists and is ACTIVE. If order doesn't exist, let it pass (keep current behavior per requirement). If order is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add two error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT` — for rejecting cancel when CONFIRMED shipment exists\n   - `ORDER_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER` — for rejecting shipment creation\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests:\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order → returns 200, order is CANCELLED, CREATED shipments are CANCELLED\n   - Cancel an already CANCELLED order → returns 200, succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment → returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT, order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged\n   - Cancel non-existent order → returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test:\n   - Create shipment for CANCELLED order → returns 409 with ORDER_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n- Use string status instead of enum: Rejected because Shipment already uses enum for status consistency and type safety\n- Add cancel endpoint to service layer: Rejected because controllers already contain business logic (see OrderController.create)\n- Make OrderRepository return shipments: Rejected because ShipmentRepository is the source of truth for shipments\n- Add database transaction: Rejected because ticket says in-memory fixture and no new dependencies allowed\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel — Happy path (ACTIVE → CANCELLED):**\n   - Request: orderId in URL\n   - Find order in OrderRepository → Order(status=ACTIVE)\n   - Query shipments via ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId\n   - If any shipment.status == CONFIRMED → throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT), status 409\n   - Update order.status = CANCELLED, save to OrderRepository\n   - Update all shipments with status=CREATED to status=CANCELLED, save to ShipmentRepository\n   - Response: 200 OK, body: Order with status=CANCELLED\n\n2. **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel — Idempotent (already CANCELLED):**\n   - Find order → Order(status=CANCELLED)\n   - Query shipments → check for CONFIRMED (none expected, but check anyway)\n   - Order already CANCELLED, update it again to CANCELLED (no-op)\n   - Response: 200 OK, body: Order with status=CANCELLED\n\n3. **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel — Conflict (CONFIRMED shipment):**\n   - Find order → Order(status=ACTIVE)\n   - Query shipments → find one with status=CONFIRMED\n   - Throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT)\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches, returns 409, body: ApiError(ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT, message)\n   - Database unchanged (order still ACTIVE, all shipments unchanged)\n\n4. **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel — Not found:**\n   - Find order → null\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches, returns 404, body: ApiError(ORDER_NOT_FOUND, message)\n\n5. **POST /shipments — For cancelled order:**\n   - Request body contains orderId\n   - Check OrderRepository.findById(orderId)\n   - If order.status == CANCELLED → throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER)\n   - If order doesn't exist → allow creation (no validation)\n   - Otherwise create as normal\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest:\n- Test 1: Cancel ACTIVE order with no shipments → 200, order status is CANCELLED\n- Test 2: Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipment → 200, order and shipment both CANCELLED\n- Test 3: Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED and CONFIRMED shipments → 409, nothing changed\n- Test 4: Cancel already CANCELLED order → 200, idempotent (no error)\n- Test 5: Cancel non-existent order → 404, error envelope correct\n\nShipmentControllerTest:\n- Test 6: Create shipment for CANCELLED order → 409, error code correct\n- Test 7: Create shipment for ACTIVE order → still works (no regression)\n- Test 8: Create shipment for non-existent order → still works (no new validation per requirement)\n\nNow I'll implement this design.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start by adding the OrderStatus enum to Order.kt:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":937,"cache_read_input_tokens":20288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":937},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7790064-e74c-4b40-991c-fd095e7166ae","uuid":"295f6255-32f8-448f-89c3-377ef72c2f24","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:08:33.483Z","request_id":"req_011CfZuu545YukVbYWXfseAk"}
