uirement for cancel endpoint, needed to query shipments by order |\n| OrderRepository.kt | Unchanged | Correct — no changes needed |\n| ShipmentRepository.kt | Added findByOrderId method | YES — required to find shipments for an order during cancel |\n| ShipmentController.kt | Added order validation before creating shipment | YES — requirement to reject shipment creation for cancelled order |\n| ApiError.kt | Added ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT and ORDER_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER | YES — requirement for error codes |\n| OrderControllerTest.kt | Added 7 new tests for cancel endpoint | YES — requirement for tests covering all cases |\n| ShipmentControllerTest.kt | Added 3 new tests for shipment validation | YES — requirement for tests covering shipment-cancellation interaction |\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are implemented, all tests pass, all error cases are handled consistently with the existing API patterns.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add endpoint to cancel orders with status field tracking, where ACTIVE orders transition to CANCELLED, cancelling CREATED shipments, rejecting cancellations with CONFIRMED shipments (409) with all-or-nothing semantics, supporting idempotent repeated cancellations, and preventing shipment creation on CANCELLED orders.\n\nChanged:\n- `Order.kt` — Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field with default ACTIVE\n- `OrderController.kt` — Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with transaction-like semantics (all-or-nothing)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Added findByOrderId method to query shipments by order ID\n- `ShipmentController.kt` — Added validation to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders\n- `ApiError.kt` — Added ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT and ORDER_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER error codes\n- `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Added 7 new tests covering cancel scenarios: active→cancelled, idempotency, conflict with CONFIRMED shipment, not found, multiple CREATED shipments\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Added 3 new tests covering shipment creation with cancelled/active orders and non-existent order behavior\n\nTests:\n- Cancel ACTIVE order → 200, status becomes CANCELLED\n- Cancel already CANCELLED order → 200, idempotent (succeeds, no change)\n- Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment → 409 ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT, nothing changes\n- Cancel non-existent order → 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n- Cancel order with CREATED shipment → 200, both order and shipment cancelled\n- Cancel order with multiple CREATED shipments → 200, all cancelled\n- Create shipment for CANCELLED order → 409 ORDER_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER\n- Create shipment for ACTIVE order → 201, still works (no regression)\n- Create shipment for non-existent order → 201, still works (no new validation)\n\nVerification: `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ executed successfully with BUILD SUCCESS. All 23 tests passed: 11 OrderControllerTest (4 original + 7 new), 8 ShipmentControllerTest (5 original + 3 new), 3 CustomerControllerTest, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests. Zero failures, zero errors.\n\nNot done: Nothing — all acceptance criteria satisfied, all existing tests pass, all new tests pass, build passes, no forbidden files changed, no new dependencies added.","ttft_ms":2743,"type":"result","duration_ms":171894,"uuid":"6fcc807d-0a68-4c28-a213-bac08f327c61","ttft_stream_ms":565,"time_to_request_ms":25,"first_content_frame_ms":565,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

